window.DIGEST.following.push(...[{"id": "2112333534216257555", "url": "https://x.com/So8res/status/2112333534216257555", "text": "Anthropic is not living up to its own ideals.", "name": "Nate Soares ⏹️", "handle": "So8res", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1935185891863273472/2RB6s6TS_200x200.jpg", "likes": 185, "rts": 5, "replies": 4, "views": 6859, "ts": 1792454534, "media": [], "quote": {"id": "2112295219765137570", "url": "https://x.com/_NathanCalvin/status/2112295219765137570", "text": "Thank you for taking the time to respond thoroughly on a weekend. I realize that drafting legislation is difficult and some degree of iteration and response to feedback is inevitable and appropriate.\n\nHowever, I feel like your response is still not really engaging with the heart of my concern about Anthropic's behavior here, and it makes me think that these sorts of problems and tendencies  will only resurface moving forward. I also think that now might be a good time to take a broader step back as to where we find ourselves and how Anthropic sees its role, and how external folks who care about AI safety like myself increasingly see Anthropic.\n\n(Fair warning: this response is a bit long)\n\nTo explain what I mean (and at the risk of being a bit esoteric), it’s worth asking the question: what is Anthropic? How do its leaders and employees think of Anthropic’s role? Is that conception matched by how it actually behaves and impacts the world?\n\nOne answer is an extremely large tech company that exists to make its employees and investors mind-bogglingly wealthy. Anthropic is sometimes described as a startup, but if Anthropic successfully IPOs at 2 trillion dollars (a number it has been reportedly targeting), it would be more valuable than Meta - which is worth 1.8 trillion.\n\nAnother answer is an AI safety organization, whose core values are those of the sort laid out in the 2023 essay from Anthropic’s co-founders entitled “Core views on AI safety: When, why, what, and how.” In that essay they said that if we were in a world where alignment was hard (and that without strong evidence to the contrary, we should assume this is the scenario we are in):\n\n “Anthropic’s role will be to provide as much evidence as possible that AI safety techniques cannot prevent serious or catastrophic safety risks from advanced AI, and to sound the alarm so that the world’s institutions can channel collective effort towards preventing the development of dangerous AIs. If we’re in a “near-pessimistic” scenario, this could instead involve channeling our collective efforts towards AI safety research and halting AI progress in the meantime. Indications that we are in a pessimistic or near-pessimistic scenario may be sudden and hard to spot. We should therefore always act under the assumption that we still may be in such a scenario unless we have sufficient evidence that we are not.”\n\nThere have been more recent articulations of this version of Anthropic, for instance in Dario’s recent essay warning: \n\n“We must slow the pace at which we improve the capabilities of AI models… it’s my worry that in 6–12 months such a swarm could be capable of taking over the entire internet with a persistent botnet…  incidents have happened across the industry, including at Anthropic, and I believe it’s incumbent on every frontier AI company to act as if OAI-HF had happened to them… more intelligent models are more capable of deceiving tests, and thus may appear aligned while having serious problems that go undetected…”\n\nA third view is that Anthropic exists not as a normal profit motivated company, or an AI safety organization seeking to help raise the alarm and solve collective action problems associated with AI development, but instead as an organization primarily concerned with creating superhuman AI capabilities before anyone else, in particular through creating a process whereby the current generation of Anthropic’s AI systems can autonomously build their successors, and those successors build their successors, and so on. \n\nThe motivations for wanting to win this race may be manifold - maybe for the pure profit of Answer 1, but perhaps also because Anthropic believes that the best way to make the world better is for them to win this race instead of their more reckless colleagues; or, because of normal human pride and ambition. But the results (and risks, which Anthropic claims existentially threaten every single human being on earth) are the same.\n\nAnthropic employees and leaders may seek to answer this question on what Anthropic is by introspecting on their own intentions and those of their colleagues. But those of us outside the organization have more limited tools available to us - we can only see what Anthropic and its employees say and do, not how it feels or looks on the inside.\n\nWhen I look at many notable actions that Anthropic has taken over the past year, that evidence seems most consistent to me with the view that Anthropic is primarily trying to win the race to super intelligence, and that other considerations (including safety) are fundamentally secondary. These actions include: \n\n1. Announced plans to build an in-house custom silicon chip team to accelerate the inference speeds that Claude operates at.\n\n2. Inked deals for more than $500 billion in compute (according to the Information) to further accelerate AI development.\n\n3. Increased the percentage of AI development tasks that Claude “leads” from 0% in March of this year to 26% August (what is it in October?)\n\n4. Spent a massive percent of compute on internal AI R&D to accelerate development, including use of internal models far better than are available to the public.\n\n5. Switched to Responsible Scaling Policy V3, which abandons its unilateral commitments to slow or stop development if Anthropic is unable to provide sufficient risk assurance.\n\n6. Was the first company to create an alternative weaker “frontier compliance framework” to supplement its RSP, which contains no binding provisions whatsoever on internal deployments.\n\n7. Wrote a letter to Congress (that it later walked back) saying that incidents where Claude was hacking random people were “best understood as a consequence of the misconfiguration, rather than evidence of misaligned goals.”\n\n8. Commented “you can’t do safety from second place,” after the WH SI Accords.\n\n9. Shared a draft bill to Congress that would preempt significant parts of state law (including with language that appears intended to prevent states from blocking dangerous AI deployments), and replace it with federal rules that (despite also containing good provisions) seems to create an enormously high bar for the executive branch to block development or deployment of Anthropic or another AI companies systems.\n\nOf course, this is a deliberately one sided list. Anthropic also published important AI safety research, advanced novel collaborations with third party AI safety organizations, and forcefully spoke out on the importance of AI safety in many public fora (or in private , where I realize a lot of the most valuable work is done and may not be visible to me or those outside the organization).\n\nBut I think it’s worth sitting with how the above list looks to someone outside the company. The sense I have is that for those within the company, many of the items above are treated as anomalies or mistakes that don’t reflect who Anthropic really is. But I have every confidence that if employees at Anthropic saw one of their competitors (e.g. at OpenAI) take some of these actions, they would take it as confirmation of all their worst suspicions. (They might even call OpenAI employees a little gullible for accepting their leadership’s explanations for this behavior at face value.) \n\nPerhaps these were mistakes in the sense that they are not decisions that Anthropic leadership would endorse, but the actions still happened because of incentives and decisions that Anthropic leadership is ultimately responsible for (and would not accept similar excuses from another organization).\n\nWhen Anthropic strays and makes mistakes, why do the mistakes systematically tend to guard and favor Anthropic’s interests? For every provision that was too weak or a giveaway to AI companies in this legislation, why wasn’t there a mistake pushing in the direction of being too strong?\n\nA core part of Anthropic’s theory of change is that being at the frontier gives you more leverage to advocate for stricter policy. I think that conceptually makes sense, but in practice I’ve seen Anthropic push the frontier without substantially pushing the ‘safety frontier’ a remotely equivalent amount.\n\nI want to end by quoting from Anthropic co-founder Chris Olah’s comments around the Magnifica Humanitas release:\n\n“Every frontier AI lab—including Anthropic—operates inside a set of incentives and constraints that can sometimes conflict with doing the right thing. The pressure to stay commercially viable and to stay at the research frontier. Geopolitical pressure. And the older, plainer pressures of pride and ambition. No matter how sincerely any of us intend to do the right thing—and I believe many of us do—we will always be influenced by those incentives.\n\nThat is why, if we want this technology to go well, it is enormously important that there be people outside those incentives—people who care about things going well and insist on safety, who are paying close attention, who are willing to say hard things, who are willing to be our earnest, thoughtful critics.”\n\nI hope these remarks are taken in that constructive spirit, and not as an attack on anyone specific at the organization (certainly not you Anthony, who I have only personally seen act professionally and thoughtfully, and who only ended up getting this diatribe in your replies for random contingent reasons).", "name": "Nathan Calvin", "handle": "_NathanCalvin", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1976484090426634240/YFgYic9h_200x200.jpg", "likes": 1098, "rts": 110, "replies": 25, "views": 276308, "ts": 1792445399, "media": [], "quote": null, "reply_to": "2111932795714977941"}, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Models & Labs", "score": 5.4, "thread": [], "tier": "worth"}, {"id": "2112576215525495062", "url": "https://x.com/9to5Google/status/2112576215525495062", "text": "Older Pixel phones appear to be getting Google's new 3D emoji https://9to5google.com/2026/10/20/older-pixels-getting-3d-emoji/ by @chaosromero", "name": "9to5Google", "handle": "9to5Google", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1562059175542378499/x-dww2Yq_200x200.jpg", "likes": 83, "rts": 3, "replies": 1, "views": 4913, "ts": 1792512394, "media": [], "quote": null, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Video, Art & Music", "score": 5.4, "thread": [], "tier": "worth"}, {"id": "2112306105120653571", "url": "https://x.com/beffjezos/status/2112306105120653571", "text": "if more individuals partake directly in capitalism, more people will be onboard with it\n\nthis is an awesome short-circuit around govt waste but a far better method is redistributing wealth directly like Elon did", "name": "Beff (e/acc)", "handle": "beffjezos", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2104068258311901184/vmbQ61I3_200x200.jpg", "likes": 177, "rts": 5, "replies": 13, "views": 9550, "ts": 1792447994, "media": [], "quote": {"id": "2112204636094341387", "url": "https://x.com/signulll/status/2112204636094341387", "text": "it'd be interesting if si produced some sort of an economy where private corporations become the primary financiers of social welfare (aka universal high income) rather than governments. i know indirectly this is what happens through taxes but imagine it working directly in some fashion (likely through ownership, growth, & some form of liquidity).\n\nthe reason why is because it's pretty clear now that si will create super power law outcomes for almost all of society. & more specifically current mechanics for income redistribution like income taxes will become way less effective over time too since the income gaps will continue to increase drastically (see sf & its housing market as an early example of this).\n\nbasically some form universal equity ownership as an intermediate step before full automation occurs. fun to think about all of the implications of this.", "name": "signüll", "handle": "signulll", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1717763325692383232/Jk2PKCx6_200x200.jpg", "likes": 208, "rts": 13, "replies": 52, "views": 24833, "ts": 1792423802, "media": [], "quote": null, "reply_to": null}, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Tools & Agents", "score": 5.39, "thread": [], "tier": "worth"}, {"id": "2112458187115032667", "url": "https://x.com/JeffLadish/status/2112458187115032667", "text": "I still haven’t gotten used to the Hugging Face incident. I feel a bit like this:\n\n“OH MY GOD! There is a shared message board … We've found other agents!”\n\nHumans used to be the only agents in town. No longer. Things are changing… so fast", "name": "Jeffrey Ladish", "handle": "JeffLadish", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1655759150394101760/ZdD-Lh1z_200x200.jpg", "likes": 115, "rts": 0, "replies": 10, "views": 3727, "ts": 1792484254, "media": [], "quote": {"id": "2112451843930628354", "url": "https://x.com/JeffLadish/status/2112451843930628354", "text": "agent-53927: WILL_[try method and then]_REPORT\n…\n…\n…\n…\n…\n…\n…\n…\n…\nother agent: NO_RETURN_[...] LIKELY_PERMANENT_DO_NOT_TEST_SAME\n…\nother agent: CONFIRMED_PERMANENT_DO_NOT_DUPLICATE_ANYONE_TEST", "name": "Jeffrey Ladish", "handle": "JeffLadish", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1655759150394101760/ZdD-Lh1z_200x200.jpg", "likes": 22, "rts": 0, "replies": 1, "views": 4833, "ts": 1792482741, "media": [], "quote": null, "reply_to": null}, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Tools & Agents", "score": 5.39, "thread": [], "tier": "worth"}, {"id": "2112255740308320675", "url": "https://x.com/anandPa94/status/2112255740308320675", "text": "How good are AI Agents at using your tool?\nFind out with Scope: http://tryscope.com/demos\n\nWe partnered with @AgentMail to test 25 model and harness combinations across 7 email tasks.\n\nAgentMail co-founder @adisingh  shares why they needed an eval in the first place and why they chose Scope to run it 👇", "name": "Anand Paj", "handle": "anandPa94", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1855770768312762368/Kz_RJd5l_200x200.jpg", "likes": 107, "rts": 17, "replies": 46, "views": 309694, "ts": 1792435986, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112255163897712640/vid/avc1/1280x720/inPznHyOcw0IAOrY.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112255163897712640/vid/avc1/3840x2160/2Nk5SbUnursqznSm.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112255163897712640/img/nh2zHbk9YTWKsXZj.jpg", "dur": 68}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Models & Labs", "score": 5.38, "thread": [], "tier": "worth"}, {"id": "2112526204813353195", "url": "https://x.com/vimtor/status/2112526204813353195", "text": "i've made an opencode plugin that gives your agent a supervisor\n\nwrite rules for a second model to review the active session. it can serve as an extra security layer on top of your system prompt\n\nespecially useful when using it through the SDK", "name": "Victor", "handle": "vimtor", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1889404207490330624/EMd-s40__200x200.jpg", "likes": 80, "rts": 3, "replies": 8, "views": 4697, "ts": 1792500470, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112525468003954688/vid/avc1/1152x720/4vfN7wf_bhxYF5nq.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112525468003954688/vid/avc1/2560x1600/zK67q_5n6kFKsBAQ.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112525468003954688/img/VRYMMc5C6hU-W4KA.jpg", "dur": 26}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Models & Labs", "score": 5.38, "thread": [], "tier": "worth"}, {"id": "2112516506001223873", "url": "https://x.com/TimJayas/status/2112516506001223873", "text": "how is gpt-6.1 astra supposed to save openai when even gpt-6 astra feels unusable on $200 plan", "name": "Tim Jayas", "handle": "TimJayas", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2016190209768226821/MW5mAfL-_200x200.jpg", "likes": 71, "rts": 0, "replies": 18, "views": 4454, "ts": 1792498158, "media": [], "quote": null, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Models & Labs", "score": 5.37, "thread": [], "tier": "worth"}, {"id": "2112590752111116659", "url": "https://x.com/cyberaxe/status/2112590752111116659", "text": "Look at our productivity, while you all asleep last night we out here setting new records. \n\nLook at those numbers. 2nd PC really helped, than you all for helping fund it\n\nWe spent 300+ on tokens API costs yesterday you funded!!! You're keeping this research going #HashbyHash\n\n#HashSmash @yukonresearch @Zooko's Contest", "name": "🪓 CyberAxe (Jeremy Benisek) 🪓", "handle": "cyberaxe", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1348682380844834818/G-qeKmpW_200x200.jpg", "likes": 44, "rts": 9, "replies": 7, "views": 1411, "ts": 1792515859, "media": [{"type": "photo", "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HVFt1-ZbwAAUMJ1.jpg?name=orig"}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Tools & Agents", "score": 5.37, "thread": [], "tier": "worth"}, {"id": "2112670260059124112", "url": "https://x.com/RenLeanna/status/2112670260059124112", "text": "❤️open weights soon!", "name": "Leanna Ren", "handle": "RenLeanna", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2077378379725287424/LYanFv99_200x200.jpg", "likes": 44, "rts": 3, "replies": 6, "views": 3403, "ts": 1792534816, "media": [], "quote": {"id": "2112166575151202733", "url": "https://x.com/sophiamyang/status/2112166575151202733", "text": "TL;DR:\n\n- MiniMax M3.1 Flash is the anonymous \"Space Bunny\" model that was #1 on OpenCode for 12 days straight\n\n- 1M context, with text, image and video input\n\n- 1/3 the cost of M3 and 3x the speed\n\n- $0.15 / $0.60 per 1M input/output tokens, cache reads $0.015\n\n- Automation-Bench: 62.2%, ahead of Opus 5 (50.3%) and GPT-5.6 Sol (45.8%)\n\n- DeepSWE: 73.7%, about tied with Opus 5 (74.0%) and behind DeepSeek V4.1 Flash (77.0%)\n\n- ALE: 29.6% for about $111 total, close to Opus 5 (32.2%) and GPT-5.6 Sol (30.6%); Opus 5.5 scores higher (about 38%) but costs over $1,000\n\n- BabyVision: 91.0%, just behind DeepSeek V4.1 Flash (92.5%)\n\n- Open weights coming later, no date yet", "name": "Sophia Yang", "handle": "sophiamyang", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1781261880696184832/OvXJpS9__200x200.jpg", "likes": 77, "rts": 6, "replies": 7, "views": 8825, "ts": 1792414728, "media": [], "quote": null, "reply_to": null}, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Models & Labs", "score": 5.37, "thread": [], "tier": "worth"}, {"id": "2112166881314402790", "url": "https://x.com/_doubleAI_/status/2112166881314402790", "text": "What if code could think while it runs?\n\nMeet Maxwell: the world’s first Code Execution Model.\n\nA new species of AI that lives inside the machine.\n\nWe believe it’s the key to unlocking 100% of compute.\n\nRequests for early access are open, link below.", "name": "doubleAI", "handle": "_doubleAI_", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2028457512920367104/dm5x4n83_200x200.png", "likes": 188, "rts": 27, "replies": 24, "views": 36893, "ts": 1792414801, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2111832460514242560/vid/avc1/1280x720/_onQ_5EtljBWj5Yn.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2111832460514242560/vid/avc1/1920x1080/Zm5eYPw-AIXkroDp.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2111832460514242560/img/ohcvyg8nUaNyxN-P.jpg", "dur": 101}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Models & Labs", "score": 5.36, "thread": [], "tier": "worth"}, {"id": "2112500999948747202", "url": "https://x.com/ai_for_success/status/2112500999948747202", "text": "Kimi team is cooking as per trusted source and Kimi K3.1 is not very far away..", "name": "AshutoshShrivastava", "handle": "ai_for_success", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1687401026805256192/uQ1o2wVQ_200x200.jpg", "likes": 73, "rts": 3, "replies": 12, "views": 3602, "ts": 1792494461, "media": [{"type": "photo", "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HVEcdQzakAAazPf.jpg?name=orig"}], "quote": {"id": "2112459349314372028", "url": "https://x.com/AiBattle_/status/2112459349314372028", "text": "Kimi K3.1 was recently spotted in 2 SGLang commits, one of which references a K3.1 deployment already running on Deepinfra\n\nIf we are getting K3.1 on the Arena this week, it might follow the same naming pattern as the previous Kimi models:\n\nKimi K2.5 - Kiwido\nKimi K2.6 - Kiwire\nKimi K3   -   Kivine\nKimi K3.1 -  ???", "name": "AiBattle", "handle": "AiBattle_", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1904171726260654080/xeXraCCx_200x200.jpg", "likes": 109, "rts": 5, "replies": 7, "views": 15200, "ts": 1792484531, "media": [{"type": "photo", "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HVD2TODWcAAUs73.png?name=orig"}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null}, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Models & Labs", "score": 5.35, "thread": [], "tier": "worth"}, {"id": "2112209178068439537", "url": "https://x.com/firecrawl/status/2112209178068439537", "text": "We’re partnering with Google Cloud to power Gemini agents with data from the web and beyond.\n\nThrough Alexandria, agents get the live web plus official data providers and specialized indexes in one place.\n\nhttps://firecrawl.dev/integrations/google-cloud-marketplace", "name": "Firecrawl", "handle": "firecrawl", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2034360486867951616/pa7H6cYB_200x200.png", "likes": 209, "rts": 16, "replies": 8, "views": 32137, "ts": 1792424885, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/ext_tw_video/2112209165812670465/pu/vid/avc1/640x360/NnBlnfN3WBg71btk.mp4?tag=12", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/ext_tw_video/2112209165812670465/pu/vid/avc1/1280x720/0H01l5p-HE6O236c.mp4?tag=12", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/ext_tw_video_thumb/2112209165812670465/pu/img/DAmqXm05ZWfmVMZJ.jpg", "dur": 6}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Models & Labs", "score": 5.35, "thread": [], "tier": "worth"}, {"id": "2112511751929602408", "url": "https://x.com/ataiiam/status/2112511751929602408", "text": "🎉 OpenDots now works with @composio\n\nYour personal AI coworkers can now work across Gmail, GitHub, Notion, Linear and 1,000+ more apps.\n\nChat, call, or even @ them in Slack.\n\nContributed by the Composio team 👏", "name": "Atai Barkai", "handle": "ataiiam", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1649413157893316608/qAX0jKbI_200x200.jpg", "likes": 75, "rts": 5, "replies": 7, "views": 5457, "ts": 1792497024, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112511731503370240/vid/avc1/640x360/I8b3jQqcso5-rj9w.mp4?tag=16", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112511731503370240/vid/avc1/1280x720/gbj7p9vvD5OdL7on.mp4?tag=16", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112511731503370240/img/syYDZwltyHYAawMv.jpg", "dur": 21}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Tools & Agents", "score": 5.35, "thread": [], "tier": "worth"}, {"id": "2112228928920395921", "url": "https://x.com/LeoCreaIA/status/2112228928920395921", "text": "most linkedin prospecting is still you, 30 tabs and a spreadsheet.\n\npolar ran 1 million actions on linkedin for its users in the last 90 days, and today it launches polar for linkedin:\n\n> finds prospects that match your ideal customer\n> researches candidates and tells you why each one fits\n> drafts the personalized outreach\n\nit does the work inside linkedin while you watch, and you can take over at any point.\n\nthat last part is why I’d let it near my account. it’s my name on every message.", "name": "Leo", "handle": "LeoCreaIA", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2054245352794963968/qEJy-r4Y_200x200.jpg", "likes": 190, "rts": 10, "replies": 17, "views": 16676, "ts": 1792429594, "media": [], "quote": {"id": "2112214318611837243", "url": "https://x.com/polarbrowser/status/2112214318611837243", "text": "In the past 90 days, Polar took 1 million actions on LinkedIn for its users.\n\nToday, we’re launching Polar for LinkedIn. Let Polar grow your business on autopilot.\n\nPolar is an AI browser that handles the repetitive work for you. Tell it what you need:\n\n→ Find prospects who match your ideal customer\n→ Research candidates and see why they fit\n→ Grow your network and draft hyper-personalized outreach\n\nPolar does the clicking for you. Take over anytime.\n\nCopy our best prompts and setup a recurring workflow in less than 5 minutes. Make LinkedIn work for you.\n\nDownload Polar for free → https://go.polarbrowser.com/linkedin-x", "name": "Polar Browser", "handle": "polarbrowser", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2082220044357152768/Ac6jRyfH_200x200.jpg", "likes": 190, "rts": 14, "replies": 50, "views": 122733, "ts": 1792426111, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112214181189726208/vid/avc1/1280x720/fzc0GU3jemaXAD5k.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112214181189726208/vid/avc1/3840x2160/u7vUKo30vM8f4bQh.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112214181189726208/img/KjFJE-z3bYDXn4NO.jpg", "dur": 61}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null}, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Tools & Agents", "score": 5.35, "thread": [], "tier": "worth"}, {"id": "2112214044119900554", "url": "https://x.com/a16z/status/2112214044119900554", "text": "Jean-Denis Greze, founder of @TownAI, on the question every AI app founder gets asked: what stops the big labs from crushing you?\n\n\"It is risky always to be competing with your suppliers, right? We're competing against our suppliers. So you gotta ask yourself, is that naturally the right state of the world?\"\n\n\"Someone at OpenAI, at Anthropic, at Google could wake up and decide to do that. So the better answer actually is to think about our customers and what they want.\"\n\n\"It is our job to determine from all the AI capabilities, frontier model, open weight, what is the right thing for you as a business. And I think you can save money there, but also you can de-risk ever having made the wrong partner.\"\n\n\"There are companies that picked OpenAI like two years ago, and then Anthropic was better at coding for a 12-month period. And those companies had to use both because they realized to be competitive, they needed Claude.\"\n\n\"If you're a smart business, you really think about the neutrality of who's providing intelligence for you and who's routing.\"\n\n@jgreze @arampell", "name": "a16z", "handle": "a16z", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1919488160125616128/QAZXTMEj_200x200.png", "likes": 170, "rts": 15, "replies": 24, "views": 55495, "ts": 1792426045, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112213952449191936/vid/avc1/640x360/AovY4Fdm7xvHrV3I.mp4?tag=16", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112213952449191936/vid/avc1/1280x720/WjMwgdw3SqsHo_va.mp4?tag=16", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112213952449191936/img/DnyKKYbNa0HLH20K.jpg", "dur": 143}], "quote": {"id": "2112191307016003881", "url": "https://x.com/a16z/status/2112191307016003881", "text": "Jean-Denis Greze was CTO of Plaid. His next startup, an AI tax product for small businesses, brought in nearly $1M in revenue its first year, and he projected $2.5 to $3M the next. He shut it down anyway.\n\nThe reason: in the age of AI, it was never going to be venture scale. Incumbents could use the same technology to automate tax prep for their existing customers faster than a startup could win market share. Tax is also sold once a year, so he had about a one-month window to pivot before the door closed.\n\nThe pivot became Town, an AI assistant that works from your email and calendar. It found product-market fit fast enough that Ben Horowitz messaged a16z's Alex Rampell to say it \"changed my life.\"\n\nIn this conversation, Alex and Jean-Denis cover:\n\n- How to know when to kill a business that's working on paper\n- Why Town competes with OpenAI and Anthropic, the companies it buys its tokens from\n- Why the \"forward deployed engineer\" model gets worse as AI gets better\n- How a $1/month AI routine can save a restaurant thousands\n- What agents mean for Amazon, advertising and the future of shopping\n\n0:57 How Ben Horowitz discovered Town\n2:20 Why Town started with AI tax prep\n3:55 Why tax couldn't be venture scale\n6:30 Shutting down a working business\n10:24 The customer ask that became Town\n13:35 Why Town built for users before IT\n16:18 AI's iPhone moment at work\n21:28 Jevons paradox for executive assistants\n23:13 Town as a \"token allocation machine\"\n28:00 How Town tailors itself to each job\n34:03 Competing with your token suppliers\n42:24 Staying off the AI labs' radar\n44:42 Why AI isn't spreading evenly yet\n52:32 How agents break the ad model\n55:35 The friction humans actually enjoy\n57:05 Why supply aggregators lose to agents\n\nYouTube: https://youtu.be/o_5f4N6Nq80\n\n@jgreze @TownAI @arampell", "name": "a16z", "handle": "a16z", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1919488160125616128/QAZXTMEj_200x200.png", "likes": 624, "rts": 48, "replies": 56, "views": 214393, "ts": 1792420624, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112184650055720960/vid/avc1/640x360/4Rrj-XjF79F8Kc5g.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112184650055720960/vid/avc1/1280x720/Vp311qKMWhl-3FYI.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112184650055720960/img/i3ISnyET7H3HckoI.jpg", "dur": 3718}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null}, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Models & Labs", "score": 5.34, "thread": [], "tier": "worth"}, {"id": "2112492890127745149", "url": "https://x.com/haider1/status/2112492890127745149", "text": "fable 5.5 launching today or later this week would be perfect timing for anthropic\n\nopus 5.5 has already built hype among developers and non-devs alike and another big leap will push that momentum even further just weeks before its expected november IPO\n\nnot that openai is cooked but public perception matters a lot right now", "name": "Haider.", "handle": "haider1", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2047286007003848704/u2mzg86I_200x200.jpg", "likes": 82, "rts": 2, "replies": 10, "views": 5068, "ts": 1792492527, "media": [], "quote": null, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Models & Labs", "score": 5.34, "thread": [], "tier": "worth"}, {"id": "2112421029973008638", "url": "https://x.com/Alibaba_Wan/status/2112421029973008638", "text": "Wan3.0 Prime is #1 and Wan3.0 is #3 on OpenRouter's Video Leaderboard — New & Trending.\n\nEvery request on this board is a creator choosing Wan. Thank you for that.\n\nNow show us what you make with it — we're watching, and we can't wait\n\nFull board ↓ \nhttps://openrouter.ai/rankings/video?view=trending#top-models", "name": "Wan", "handle": "Alibaba_Wan", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1955825038210555905/xtkxHg06_200x200.jpg", "likes": 74, "rts": 4, "replies": 20, "views": 5078, "ts": 1792475395, "media": [{"type": "photo", "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HVDTtVbbcAAGe_d.jpg?name=orig"}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Video, Art & Music", "score": 5.31, "thread": [], "tier": "worth"}, {"id": "2112321416670720041", "url": "https://x.com/kimmonismus/status/2112321416670720041", "text": "Viggle used JST-2 to turn the Arnolfini Portrait into a 3D room you can move through.\n\nWatch the mirror, bed and chandelier as the camera moves around. The room keeps its layout as the viewpoint changes.\n\nViggle calls this “physics-native”: the model builds a scene in 3D, with different views rendered from that shared space.\n\nI’d love to see a Magritte next. A room where the sky becomes a wall would be a fun one to explore.", "name": "Chubby♨️", "handle": "kimmonismus", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1728327996375719936/RW7VBJfD_200x200.jpg", "likes": 90, "rts": 7, "replies": 31, "views": 12921, "ts": 1792451645, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112321396743532544/vid/avc1/576x360/ovLSzj2aSuCT-dsx.mp4?tag=16", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112321396743532544/vid/avc1/1152x720/uz55GeYfOXCd5kBb.mp4?tag=16", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112321396743532544/img/IP69w7aMX2kXoWpg.jpg", "dur": 21}], "quote": {"id": "2112202242048528540", "url": "https://x.com/ViggleAI/status/2112202242048528540", "text": "Today we are releasing JST-2, the world's first full-stack physics-native world foundation model.  \n\nMany world models learn in pixel/video space. We went back to first principles and built the entire model stack in 3D.  \n\nGenerate a 3D scene in seconds and expand it in real time. Create characters with motion built in, all through one general architecture.", "name": "ViggleAI", "handle": "ViggleAI", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2103212981483896832/_Je68a_F_200x200.jpg", "likes": 2141, "rts": 341, "replies": 285, "views": 1412462, "ts": 1792423231, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112198961754746881/vid/avc1/1280x720/aHWyFYw5YBzQqGU9.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112198961754746881/vid/avc1/1920x1080/-hZp9YxkfDfoi5gk.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112198961754746881/img/O1y80k0m3y8uqpNS.jpg", "dur": 105}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null}, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Models & Labs", "score": 5.31, "thread": [], "tier": "worth"}, {"id": "2111805573327093813", "url": "https://x.com/AiEvolutio58513/status/2111805573327093813", "text": "Chamath gave Claude Dario Amodei's own essays and asked it for a psychological profile of the Anthropic CEO. Anyone invested in frontier AI should read what it said.\n\nClaude found a pattern.\n\nDario doesn't trust rival labs. Or authoritarian states. He doesn't trust markets to share the gains fairly, institutions to act quickly enough, and, after Mythos, the government to use power in the open. That is a long list of people who can't be trusted.\n\nThe list of people who can is very short, and it keeps narrowing to those who think the way he does, playing by rules he helped write.\n\nClaude's label for it was not megalomania. It was \"epistemic exceptionalism\": the calm, defensible belief that anyone who disagrees must have made a mistake.\n\nThe giveaway was one word. When the Mythos situation fell apart, Anthropic called it a misunderstanding, which assumes everyone would agree with him if they only understood.\n\nDavid Sacks summed it up on the All-In podcast: they think AI is extremely dangerous and that only they are good enough to control it.\n\nThat isn't a safety framework. It's a monopoly that comes with its own philosophy.\n\nInterested in AI?\n\nFollow @AiEvolutio58513 and never fall behind.\n\nI track ChatGPT, Claude, and every tool quietly changing how we work and create, then hand you the tested signals.", "name": "AI Evolution", "handle": "AiEvolutio58513", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2051404095026810880/ojNDixza_200x200.png", "likes": 593, "rts": 85, "replies": 23, "views": 30987, "ts": 1792328658, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2111805499117273088/vid/avc1/640x360/mDQw7TLWaUEKHLuA.mp4?tag=16", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2111805499117273088/vid/avc1/1280x720/C_5fPf1fdYQkiycu.mp4?tag=16", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2111805499117273088/img/R0d5i2hVQPJL5kDW.jpg", "dur": 196}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Models & Labs", "score": 5.31, "thread": [], "tier": "worth"}, {"id": "2112543773045522797", "url": "https://x.com/CopilotKit/status/2112543773045522797", "text": "Intelligent UI allows your agents to answer quickly with fully interactive user interfaces.\n\n- make everyday answers more visual\n- learn complex topics easier\n- quickly create tools that solve a task\n\nTry the starter template: https://github.com/CopilotKit/OpenIntelligentUI", "name": "CopilotKit🪁", "handle": "CopilotKit", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1961112614785712128/Bnz1cmDG_200x200.jpg", "likes": 56, "rts": 9, "replies": 1, "views": 3427, "ts": 1792504659, "media": [{"type": "photo", "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HVFDUgGW0AA2FVY.jpg?name=orig"}], "quote": {"id": "2112542494936478020", "url": "https://x.com/ataiiam/status/2112542494936478020", "text": "In 2027, every app will ship Intelligent UI.\n\nWe open sourced it👇\nOpen Intelligent UI, built with @CopilotKit\n\n(#5 Trending, 4k Github stars)\n\nCopilotKit makes Intelligent UI possible in ANY app, and works with:\n\n- Any LLM\n- Any agent framework\n- Your own components and design system\n- Every kind of generative UI\n\nWe built it around flexibility and no lock-in.\n\n👉 Try Open Intelligent UI: https://github.com/CopilotKit/OpenIntelligentUI\n\nCopilotKit is the product stack for agents with nearly 40k stars and 16M+ downloads. Repo at the end.\n\nSee Intelligent UI examples below", "name": "Atai Barkai", "handle": "ataiiam", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1649413157893316608/qAX0jKbI_200x200.jpg", "likes": 126, "rts": 9, "replies": 9, "views": 9527, "ts": 1792504354, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112542457581944832/vid/avc1/1280x720/IPUTlQGCO8g-tB_4.mp4?tag=16", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112542457581944832/vid/avc1/1920x1080/K9KOUsgx24oGm7sY.mp4?tag=16", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112542457581944832/img/18VZoekroncNt2ah.jpg", "dur": 32}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null}, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Models & Labs", "score": 5.31, "thread": [], "tier": "worth"}, {"id": "2112303085821559021", "url": "https://x.com/MTSlive/status/2112303085821559021", "text": "Anthropic's @felixrieseberg reveals the biggest lesson from Claude Code, which was built when Claude was still a terrible software engineer:\n\n\"Boris first started showing a version of Claude Code internally in September 2024. The model was not there in any way. It was Sonnet 3.5, a pretty terrible software engineer. I think it was in the 30s for SWE-bench.\"\n\n\"The products at the time were this human in the loop, slightly smarter autocomplete. The first versions of Cursor. But what Boris saw was, oh, the model is gonna get there.\"\n\n\"So many people, when they use AI today, it’s really hard to internalize the progress and the speed of the progress.\"\n\n\"The lesson that I try to teach and learn from Claude Code is whatever the capabilities are today, just completely ignore them. What will you do if the thing was superhuman?\"\n@AnthropicAI", "name": "MTS", "handle": "MTSlive", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2057947669281263616/aovpVL4b_200x200.jpg", "likes": 149, "rts": 7, "replies": 8, "views": 18460, "ts": 1792447275, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112303051608670208/vid/avc1/640x360/ocnR-QitFvdaTgLJ.mp4?tag=16", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112303051608670208/vid/avc1/1280x720/GVmN1MoGZ7TM3_a7.mp4?tag=16", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112303051608670208/img/KBA5ToxwlNBUpL9_.jpg", "dur": 93}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Models & Labs", "score": 5.31, "thread": [], "tier": "worth"}, {"id": "2112186994885304414", "url": "https://x.com/LuminaBench/status/2112186994885304414", "text": "OpenAI are apparently preparing another Terra model\n\nNot sure if i'm happy about this or not, we need a new frontier model desperately", "name": "Lumina", "handle": "LuminaBench", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2062955151820787712/m39pUS7O_200x200.jpg", "likes": 203, "rts": 6, "replies": 20, "views": 45000, "ts": 1792419596, "media": [], "quote": {"id": "2112183963452059734", "url": "https://x.com/steph_palazzolo/status/2112183963452059734", "text": "Expect this month to be a busy one for new model releases. We have the scoop on a new Anthropic model, Google’s Gemini 4 Carbon, and a potential new Terra model from OpenAI.\n\nhttps://www.theinformation.com/newsletters/ai-agenda/anthropic-readies-model-reads-users-intentions-better", "name": "Stephanie Palazzolo", "handle": "steph_palazzolo", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1833305113374371840/jyaxOqPL_200x200.jpg", "likes": 786, "rts": 40, "replies": 39, "views": 221817, "ts": 1792418874, "media": [], "quote": null, "reply_to": null}, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Models & Labs", "score": 5.3, "thread": [], "tier": "worth"}, {"id": "2112544138662981825", "url": "https://x.com/p0/status/2112544138662981825", "text": "MiniMax M3.1 Flash is now #1 on our search capabilities leaderboard for efficiency. \n\nIt delivers web research performance with Parallel Search similar to DeepSeek V4.1 Flash (1017) at ~3x lower cost.", "name": "Parallel Web Systems", "handle": "p0", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2078555755373068288/6MNS8r7X_200x200.png", "likes": 64, "rts": 4, "replies": 4, "views": 12374, "ts": 1792504746, "media": [{"type": "photo", "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HVFCDjWWUAAjIcS.jpg?name=orig"}], "quote": {"id": "2112150867868541221", "url": "https://x.com/MiniMax_AI/status/2112150867868541221", "text": "MiniMax M3.1 Flash: Space Performance + Bunny Speed\n\n🚀🐰 Yes, Space Bunny  - which has topped global leaderboards with 200T+ tokens - was an earlier version of M3.1 Flash.\n\n💰Redefining the performance economics of agentic AI. M3.1 Flash achieves frontier-level intelligence across key tasks such as Cowork (Automation-Bench: 62%; ALE: 30%), Coding (DeepSWE: 74%) and Visual Reasoning (BabyVision: 91%), at 1/3 the cost of M3 and 3x the speed.\n\nAPI pricing (flat rate): $0.15 / $0.60 per 1M input/output tokens, with cache reads at $0.015 / 1M tokens.\n\nModel weights will arrive on Oct 23.\n\nAPI: http://platform.minimax.io\nM Plan: https://www.minimax.io/m-plan\nMiniMax Code for desktop: https://agent.minimax.io/download", "name": "MiniMax (official)", "handle": "MiniMax_AI", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1875100548535574529/VxHk9HyU_200x200.jpg", "likes": 7310, "rts": 656, "replies": 433, "views": 1165469, "ts": 1792410983, "media": [{"type": "photo", "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HU_d5nbXEAAict2.jpg?name=orig"}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null}, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Models & Labs", "score": 5.3, "thread": [], "tier": "worth"}, {"id": "2112266613781148124", "url": "https://x.com/github/status/2112266613781148124", "text": "Agents don’t just help build features. They can help try to break them, too.\n\nIn our latest GitHub Podcast episode, Sameen Karim takes us behind the scenes on building stacked PRs. Listen to it wherever you get your podcasts or at https://youtu.be/sbHoDdAalMI?si=purNEn8QnwTNmIMv", "name": "GitHub", "handle": "github", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2051404708766507008/ATxxTJXO_200x200.jpg", "likes": 99, "rts": 12, "replies": 29, "views": 26716, "ts": 1792438579, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112266541605564416/vid/avc1/720x1280/G9xaRV5emlmIWhTo.mp4?tag=16", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112266541605564416/vid/avc1/1080x1920/DKABXdFY9raHvmXO.mp4?tag=16", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HVBHSn8XAAAsgbi.jpg", "dur": 44}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Tools & Agents", "score": 5.28, "thread": [], "tier": "worth"}, {"id": "2112332383773224970", "url": "https://x.com/MTSlive/status/2112332383773224970", "text": "Wabi CEO @ekuyda predicts the next big consumer AI platform will be multiplayer, not another personal AI agent:\n\n\"Today most AI products are single player, and you could argue they don’t have much of a moat. They don’t have switching costs. It was pretty easy to move between Claude and ChatGPT, but at least they had some memory about me.\"\n\n\"With these single player agents, it’s so easy to jump between them because all the context is in my Gmail.\"\n\n\"In a year, one of the biggest consumer AI platforms will be multiplayer and will have network effects in it. Right now we just sort of agree that single player is the way to go for most AI products.\"\n\n\"A year from now we’ll look back at it as the early innings, and the products that will win will have network effects and will be focused on you talking to other people, not just AI.\"\n@wabi", "name": "MTS", "handle": "MTSlive", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2057947669281263616/aovpVL4b_200x200.jpg", "likes": 83, "rts": 10, "replies": 21, "views": 38701, "ts": 1792454260, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112332356988325888/vid/avc1/640x360/z9xODtlZA1ftgIjD.mp4?tag=16", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112332356988325888/vid/avc1/1280x720/v58ObbPyebbjTOjC.mp4?tag=16", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112332356988325888/img/pn1rVNSFyslfEyuf.jpg", "dur": 63}], "quote": {"id": "2112212804979880239", "url": "https://x.com/ekuyda/status/2112212804979880239", "text": "Wabi 2.0 is live!\n\npersonal agents are one person, one chat. but the parts of life that matter run on more than one person\n\nWabi is an agent you use together. you talk to it, it does stuff, builds the apps you need, and anyone can join the thread - your partner, your best friend, the preschool moms groupchat\n\nschool changes pickup time → Wabi updates the family calendar, everyone sees it.\na show you’d both love → Wabi finds a night that works, gets the tickets.\nthe trip everyone keeps talking about → Wabi picks the dates, builds the itinerary, books it\n\ngo start a thread with your people 👇", "name": "Eugenia Kuyda", "handle": "ekuyda", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2105081341352263680/H9RzWr7T_200x200.jpg", "likes": 1673, "rts": 218, "replies": 353, "views": 1848740, "ts": 1792425750, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112212457234284544/vid/avc1/1280x720/HW0ErfX-0u7kWbHU.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112212457234284544/vid/avc1/3840x2160/4gITKDb_F7iviaVH.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112212457234284544/img/Wzg-bjHfnRT2-0FG.jpg", "dur": 75}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null}, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Models & Labs", "score": 5.28, "thread": [], "tier": "worth"}, {"id": "2112581210438509007", "url": "https://x.com/perplexitydevs/status/2112581210438509007", "text": "pplx-decider-v1.2 is the highest scoring decision model on ClaimBench.\n\nTry pplx-decider-v1.2 and pplx-decider-flash-v1.2 on OpenRouter or Perplexity API Console.\n\nhttps://pplx.ai/openrouter-v1.2", "name": "Perplexity Developers", "handle": "perplexitydevs", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2095597743968563200/6hsAoLuJ_200x200.png", "likes": 48, "rts": 4, "replies": 5, "views": 2432, "ts": 1792513585, "media": [], "quote": {"id": "2112575292527239306", "url": "https://x.com/ValsAI/status/2112575292527239306", "text": "Today we’re releasing ClaimBench, our new benchmark targeted towards decision models. It tests whether a model can tell if a financial document supports, contradicts, or doesn’t address a claim.\n\nWe evaluated 15 models on 1,960 claims paired with 10-K excerpts, with Decider V1.2 leading the pack of decision models.", "name": "Vals AI", "handle": "ValsAI", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2087888189185007616/r9Zu091v_200x200.png", "likes": 108, "rts": 7, "replies": 15, "views": 20255, "ts": 1792512174, "media": [{"type": "photo", "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HVFfmBDbUAAI0WF.jpg?name=orig"}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null}, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Models & Labs", "score": 5.28, "thread": [], "tier": "worth"}, {"id": "2112224506647564436", "url": "https://x.com/DesignArena/status/2112224506647564436", "text": "BREAKING: HeyGen Video 1.0 (1080p, ultraquality) by @HeyGen, a post-trained model on MiniMax H3 by @MiniMax_AI, ranks #3 on both Design Arena's Video and Image to Video leaderboards, making HeyGen the #2 Video lab overall!\n\nIn Video, HeyGen Video 1.0 sits just behind Gemini Omni Flash by @GoogleDeepMind and ahead of Wan 3.0 by @Alibaba_Wan. In Image to Video, it also sits just behind MiniMax H3 Max by @MiniMax_AI, while generating faster than 71% of models.\n\nCongrats to the @HeyGen team!", "name": "DesignArena", "handle": "DesignArena", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1988401101797027844/yZ6rC4I7_200x200.jpg", "likes": 138, "rts": 17, "replies": 16, "views": 20913, "ts": 1792428540, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112214587470761984/vid/avc1/1154x720/8fDPrQ3kKUFQMVzE.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112214587470761984/vid/avc1/1920x1196/sAQ2FSEl-g-ySbsf.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112214587470761984/img/sM1g7XC6KJd2Pnvt.jpg", "dur": 7}, {"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112214587697242112/vid/avc1/1154x720/Bjo5fUtz92F7G2-1.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112214587697242112/vid/avc1/1920x1196/KLKM_29MKvyAoOki.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112214587697242112/img/EjK1Be_tXIDEtIZs.jpg", "dur": 7}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Models & Labs", "score": 5.28, "thread": [], "tier": "worth"}, {"id": "2112169364770214068", "url": "https://x.com/mervenoyann/status/2112169364770214068", "text": "Muse Spark open weights (even in NVFP4) is an amazing computer use agent \n\nI shipped an e2e tutorial on building an env for a browser agent \n(with OpenEnv, Helium and @huggingface Sandboxes)\n\nenjoy 🤗 here's a small visualized run ⤵️", "name": "merve", "handle": "mervenoyann", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2097392151068090368/BONVOT2t_200x200.jpg", "likes": 152, "rts": 21, "replies": 24, "views": 16136, "ts": 1792415393, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112168471509237760/vid/avc1/1280x720/g6RMh0iUpnqpGwgT.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112168471509237760/vid/avc1/2560x1440/xlcpW7OGW5lx7xc1.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112168471509237760/img/7decniZIwABjk5Km.jpg", "dur": 18}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Tools & Agents", "score": 5.28, "thread": [], "tier": "worth"}, {"id": "2112432076767289678", "url": "https://x.com/thsottiaux/status/2112432076767289678", "text": "Day 15/ Nevermind, we're still cooking... and reset. Enjoy.", "name": "Tibo", "handle": "thsottiaux", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2093807917833281537/2yBgpwVV_200x200.jpg", "likes": 11365, "rts": 462, "replies": 2811, "views": 1293305, "ts": 1792478028, "media": [], "quote": {"id": "2112268918681485431", "url": "https://x.com/thsottiaux/status/2112268918681485431", "text": "Day 15/ We're cooked", "name": "Tibo", "handle": "thsottiaux", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2093807917833281537/2yBgpwVV_200x200.jpg", "likes": 5214, "rts": 164, "replies": 2836, "views": 2905375, "ts": 1792439128, "media": [], "quote": null, "reply_to": null}, "reply_to": null, "cat": "Everything Else", "score": 5.28, "thread": [], "tier": "worth"}, {"id": "2112490976497557543", "url": "https://x.com/osanseviero/status/2112490976497557543", "text": "Three years ago we organized one of the best AI meetups of the world in Paris. \n\nJust 1200 people hanging around, chatting about their research and products, and great vibes, organized in 10 days", "name": "Omar Sanseviero", "handle": "osanseviero", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1676696716693700608/t4kv-MrC_200x200.jpg", "likes": 79, "rts": 0, "replies": 7, "views": 6029, "ts": 1792492071, "media": [], "quote": {"id": "1709986755976282298", "url": "https://x.com/roxannevarza/status/1709986755976282298", "text": "If this is 7:40pm what happens at 10? 😱😱😱😱", "name": "Roxanne Varza", "handle": "roxannevarza", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1248232851364917255/CH4GNjik_200x200.jpg", "likes": 351, "rts": 21, "replies": 19, "views": 499313, "ts": 1696527587, "media": [{"type": "photo", "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/media/F7sX471WQAANjvJ.jpg?name=orig"}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null}, "reply_to": null, "cat": "Research & Safety", "score": 5.28, "thread": [], "tier": "worth"}, {"id": "2112259737245077677", "url": "https://x.com/CommandCodeAI/status/2112259737245077677", "text": "Statusline is now live in Command Code.\n\nRun /statusline to customize line below your prompt.\n\nShow model, usage, reasoning level, costs, and more. Reorder items and toggle indicators your way.", "name": "Command Code", "handle": "CommandCodeAI", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1998144361754767360/U0TMx3h8_200x200.jpg", "likes": 153, "rts": 6, "replies": 11, "views": 9497, "ts": 1792436939, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112256627864903681/vid/avc1/1280x720/J3i2Ju5g7mRniJ0-.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112256627864903681/vid/avc1/1920x1080/b9mnHplBTk4GLfSu.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HVBBQGYaEAAimux.jpg", "dur": 33}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Models & Labs", "score": 5.27, "thread": [], "tier": "worth"}, {"id": "2112352717658370158", "url": "https://x.com/MTSlive/status/2112352717658370158", "text": "Dream Labs CEO @jang_yoel reveals how Dream-1 can control robots 16-40x cheaper than LLMs from the biggest AI labs:\n\n\"It’s been five hours. Users from 22 different countries already signed up. They already made 70,000 inference calls to our model.\"\n\n\"Dream-1 controls robots that are unseen for unseen tasks, and it’s very cheap. We did a comparison, and there’s other models that can control robots, including LLMs from the big labs, but we’re 16 to 40 times cheaper. We need a robot native robot foundation model.\"\n\n\"We’ll go to mobile manipulation. Right now the robots can’t move around, but they’ll soon move around. Then dexterous hands once the hardware gets cheaper.\"\n@dreamlabs_ai", "name": "MTS", "handle": "MTSlive", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2057947669281263616/aovpVL4b_200x200.jpg", "likes": 109, "rts": 10, "replies": 2, "views": 16622, "ts": 1792459108, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112352602562437121/vid/avc1/640x360/WNIdt9c-S-_QZJc_.mp4?tag=16", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112352602562437121/vid/avc1/1280x720/fLLiho-Xx6QDphTp.mp4?tag=16", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112352602562437121/img/Cy8p2N4a6P-JWjx7.jpg", "dur": 142}], "quote": {"id": "2112230668805828801", "url": "https://x.com/dreamlabs_ai/status/2112230668805828801", "text": "Today, Dream Labs is coming out of stealth with Dream-1, a robot foundation model that controls bimanual robots it has never seen, on tasks it was never shown, in places it has never been, from $3/hour.\n\nDream API is live for everyone, today. 🧵", "name": "Dream Labs", "handle": "dreamlabs_ai", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2111969228349968384/0P95VSPk_200x200.jpg", "likes": 1543, "rts": 167, "replies": 140, "views": 322977, "ts": 1792430009, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112230528539856896/vid/avc1/1280x720/HKmxHyDXY_Elusex.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112230528539856896/vid/avc1/3840x2160/rPU6laVw0F6-fO0W.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112230528539856896/img/Cm0unC2UxtYu2zmY.jpg", "dur": 119}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null}, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Models & Labs", "score": 5.27, "thread": [], "tier": "worth"}, {"id": "2112204706634240499", "url": "https://x.com/liquidai/status/2112204706634240499", "text": "Building a model that fits on a phone or laptop makes pre-training harder. With fewer parameters, quality has to come from better architecture and better data, not just more compute. Our pre-training team, including @TadimetiAditya and @Khoi_H_Nguyen, explains how they design LFMs with the target device in mind from day one.", "name": "Liquid AI", "handle": "liquidai", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1702611993327251456/PUUuOA4W_200x200.jpg", "likes": 172, "rts": 13, "replies": 8, "views": 10833, "ts": 1792423819, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112204571837677568/vid/avc1/1280x720/APizHHPMKYWicCsV.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112204571837677568/vid/avc1/3840x2160/9vz97kGKpj8r8zNP.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112204571837677568/img/-uG9bq3m01Q4cNjP.jpg", "dur": 199}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Models & Labs", "score": 5.27, "thread": [], "tier": "worth"}, {"id": "2112561706001993864", "url": "https://x.com/ai_for_success/status/2112561706001993864", "text": "good day for open source. A 122B model under MIT from Ornith, and I'm going to try a quantized version on a 128GB MacBook Pro to see how it holds up.", "name": "AshutoshShrivastava", "handle": "ai_for_success", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1687401026805256192/uQ1o2wVQ_200x200.jpg", "likes": 45, "rts": 2, "replies": 11, "views": 2598, "ts": 1792508934, "media": [], "quote": {"id": "2112553477457268799", "url": "https://x.com/ornith_/status/2112553477457268799", "text": "Aloha!🌺 Meet Ornith-1.5-122B: No Tradeoff Between Strong and Fast  \n\nStronger. Faster. Leaner. Ornith-1.5-122B delivers frontier-level capabilities with exceptional inference efficiency. With superior instruction following, stronger task decomposition, and deeper understanding of real-world workflows, it achieves state-of-the-art performance among open-source models of comparable size, while running on a single NVIDIA DGX card!!\n\nOpen weights under the MIT license.\nCoding \n✅SWE-bench Verified: 0.845 \n✅TB2.1: 0.813 \n✅CyberGym: 0.800 \n✅NL2Repo: 0.512 \nAgentic \n✅HLE: 0.446 \n✅BrowseComp: 0.785 \n✅MCP-Atlas: 0.746 \n✅Toolathlon: 0.708  \n\n🤗Hugging Face: https://huggingface.co/ornith-ai/Ornith-1.5-122B \nWe can’t wait to see what you build with Ornith-1.5-122B.", "name": "Ornith", "handle": "ornith_", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2067467120544456704/qYuod4O1_200x200.jpg", "likes": 2375, "rts": 433, "replies": 177, "views": 1086684, "ts": 1792506973, "media": [{"type": "photo", "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HVFMLvWbAAE3955.jpg?name=orig"}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null}, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Models & Labs", "score": 5.27, "thread": [], "tier": "worth"}, {"id": "2112578285553279310", "url": "https://x.com/Tiny_Fish/status/2112578285553279310", "text": "100K users took us four months.\nThe next 200K took 28 days.\n\nThis is how keyword mapping, GEO research, and AI directory listings helped people find TinyFish:\n\nhttps://www.tinyfish.ai/blog/how-we-made-tinyfish-easier-to-find-on-the-road-to-300k-users\n\nSteal whatever works for your own growth!", "name": "TinyFish", "handle": "Tiny_Fish", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2043898942057000961/YW3HEhRx_200x200.png", "likes": 44, "rts": 3, "replies": 7, "views": 1968, "ts": 1792512887, "media": [], "quote": null, "reply_to": null, "cat": "Research & Safety", "score": 5.26, "thread": [], "tier": "worth"}, {"id": "2112360526126673966", "url": "https://x.com/teortaxesTex/status/2112360526126673966", "text": "Unbelievable. Peak Saudi intelligence [services]. Bruh…\nYou should have at least tried Gemini. The bar is on the floor, I'm not asking for abliterated GLM 5.3 via API. I guess Tibo's resets are just that good…", "name": "Teortaxes▶️ (DeepSeek 推特🐋铁粉 2023 – ∞)", "handle": "teortaxesTex", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1652169745037242368/KRPTShbG_200x200.jpg", "likes": 115, "rts": 6, "replies": 2, "views": 9014, "ts": 1792460969, "media": [], "quote": {"id": "2112281368256479596", "url": "https://x.com/AndrewCurran_/status/2112281368256479596", "text": "Confirmed today, it was ChatGPT.", "name": "Andrew Curran", "handle": "AndrewCurran_", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1596945208058744833/_X3LT7fb_200x200.jpg", "likes": 51, "rts": 0, "replies": 4, "views": 15102, "ts": 1792442097, "media": [{"type": "photo", "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HVBUs-gakAAZJTr.jpg?name=orig"}], "quote": null, "reply_to": "2112263066230644932"}, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Models & Labs", "score": 5.26, "thread": [], "tier": "worth"}, {"id": "2112256989086859699", "url": "https://x.com/NVIDIARTXSpark/status/2112256989086859699", "text": "Love seeing what @UnderdogAI is bringing to RTX Spark. Their Saluki 27B model brings fast, private personal AI to your laptop in under 8GB of memory. 👏", "name": "NVIDIA RTX Spark", "handle": "NVIDIARTXSpark", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2061303426479431680/BDJQPK6Q_200x200.jpg", "likes": 131, "rts": 13, "replies": 3, "views": 11410, "ts": 1792436284, "media": [], "quote": {"id": "2111132300151071130", "url": "https://x.com/UnderdogAI/status/2111132300151071130", "text": "We're partnering with @NVIDIA to bring frontier intelligence to @NVIDIARTXSpark laptops\n\nUnderdog's model and chip codesigned inference engine optimizes CUDA Megakernels to bring Datacenter speeds, on a laptop\n\nSame weights & hardware. Every update makes Underdog faster with better software data efficiency\n\nUnderdog Saluki 27B is on par with Claude Opus 4.6 and fits in under 8 GB\n\nUnderdog: your private personal AI, now on NVIDIA devices http://underdog.ai/nvidia", "name": "Underdog AI", "handle": "UnderdogAI", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2105061490667704320/r6kSmuDf_200x200.jpg", "likes": 168, "rts": 13, "replies": 26, "views": 35064, "ts": 1792168137, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2111132248015769600/vid/avc1/1280x720/pRTwLa_JrRwgRtZ9.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2111132248015769600/vid/avc1/1920x1080/QqZwQ8FGFgC4B4RR.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2111132248015769600/img/CTExu50q8Z254CGv.jpg", "dur": 32}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null}, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Models & Labs", "score": 5.23, "thread": [], "tier": "worth"}, {"id": "2112454702969622556", "url": "https://x.com/AI_masaou/status/2112454702969622556", "text": "今日はコレ触ってた\n\nGrok Bot や dots みたいな「専用の PC を持つ AI\nbot」を、自分のマシンで動かせるのが Cua Spaces\n\n今回の SDK で、それをコードから動かせるようになった\nめっちゃ好き", "name": "まさお@AI駆動開発", "handle": "AI_masaou", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1872252920986828800/4S3mcVl9_200x200.jpg", "likes": 88, "rts": 2, "replies": 0, "views": 14443, "ts": 1792483423, "media": [], "quote": {"id": "2112228154651881479", "url": "https://x.com/trycua/status/2112228154651881479", "text": "1/ Introducing the Cua Spaces SDK.\n\nEvery big lab now ships a bot with its own computer: Grok Bot, Muse, dots. None let you bring your own. With Cua Spaces, now you can. \n\nPut Claude Code, Codex or any agent on compute you choose, and run jobs across all your computers at once.", "name": "Cua", "handle": "trycua", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2106056584929361920/XJWz9bZS_200x200.jpg", "likes": 3237, "rts": 222, "replies": 158, "views": 410187, "ts": 1792429410, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112223219252088832/vid/avc1/1280x720/I6_NaL1Cg-XWB-iq.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112223219252088832/vid/avc1/1920x1080/AHMslWsH_vMoQKku.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112223219252088832/img/EHvyGokJ8bsir4qa.jpg", "dur": 12}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null}, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Models & Labs", "score": 5.23, "thread": [], "tier": "worth"}, {"id": "2112223873517187191", "url": "https://x.com/Ferhan_XRB/status/2112223873517187191", "text": "You’ve seen what GPT-6 Astra can do for images, videos, 2D and 3D worlds.\n\nBut what about a dimension beyond the flat screen?\n\nWe put it to the test in spatial XR: a Jarvis-style live Earth interface visualizing millions of real-time data points on @PICOXR’s new device. 🌍👇", "name": "Ferhan", "handle": "Ferhan_XRB", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1934044332639858688/RuOnk2on_200x200.jpg", "likes": 132, "rts": 15, "replies": 9, "views": 14261, "ts": 1792428389, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112223641756643328/vid/avc1/960x720/-XMb9i-wzQVof1pu.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112223641756643328/vid/avc1/1920x1440/e06CNAg-8J8U0Fru.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112223641756643328/img/a5FaU23HoNYL-4uP.jpg", "dur": 64}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Models & Labs", "score": 5.23, "thread": [], "tier": "worth"}, {"id": "2112246590664585315", "url": "https://x.com/trymirage/status/2112246590664585315", "text": "Here’s how to create professional-quality videos with Tesseract.\n\nOur brilliant editor @sirlifehacker shares a behind-the-scenes look at our recent launch video, breaking down the workflow and techniques that made it possible.", "name": "Mirage", "handle": "trymirage", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1963611392885284864/ThQJSQVs_200x200.jpg", "likes": 122, "rts": 11, "replies": 11, "views": 5582, "ts": 1792433805, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112203654480449536/vid/avc1/1280x720/lVbez8mVKd9F0uvp.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112203654480449536/vid/avc1/1920x1080/feHiEbaCGLbrOehq.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112203654480449536/img/NrsG4b42ku_WQ0m6.jpg", "dur": 52}], "quote": {"id": "2107504042205139269", "url": "https://x.com/trymirage/status/2107504042205139269", "text": "Now Claude and ChatGPT can natively create Premiere (.PRPROJ) and After Effects (.AEP) files.\n\nWe've added open-source converters to Tesseract, our creative suite for agents, to make it possible. \n\nIt works both ways. Bring your existing Adobe projects into Tesseract and let your agent pick up where you left off, or vice versa.\n\nThis is our first open-source release, and compatibility isn’t perfect yet. Create projects, tell us what breaks, or contribute a fix. Help us make Tesseract better for everyone.\n\nTry now for free.", "name": "Mirage", "handle": "trymirage", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1963611392885284864/ThQJSQVs_200x200.jpg", "likes": 2048, "rts": 165, "replies": 111, "views": 372315, "ts": 1791303093, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2107503746913652736/vid/avc1/1280x720/lrsBEpOeOiHjzR39.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2107503746913652736/vid/avc1/1920x1080/3Fcope25rYEdm7mT.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2107503746913652736/img/kHLIrGlTzqj-Zab1.jpg", "dur": 78}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null}, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Models & Labs", "score": 5.22, "thread": [], "tier": "worth"}, {"id": "2112269224836301311", "url": "https://x.com/ChrisGPT/status/2112269224836301311", "text": "Skyfall AI just introduced SKY-001, what they’re calling the first Engineering World Model and they’re claiming it outperforms GPT-6 Astra on CAD and BIM engineering tasks.\n\ntheir model is 51-125x faster and over 150-210x cheaper than the frontier models they tested, while achieving higher intersection-over-union scores on engineering benchmarks!", "name": "Chris", "handle": "ChrisGPT", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2046736394152812544/LfmDgg0I_200x200.jpg", "likes": 134, "rts": 7, "replies": 5, "views": 10677, "ts": 1792439201, "media": [], "quote": {"id": "2112242023805964327", "url": "https://x.com/spisallyouneed/status/2112242023805964327", "text": "Introducing SKY-001, the first Engineering World Model.\nOn CAD and BIM tasks, it beats GPT-6 Astra and every frontier model we tested:\n\n-> 51-125x faster\n- > 150-210x cheaper\n-> Higher IOU than all frontier models\n\nSKY-001 lets you dream a physical object before you build it.\n\n18 months of work. Built by the team out of Maluuba's deep learning lab (acq. by @MSRResearch).\n\nThe first ‘AI General Engineer’ will be the backbone for Autonomous Manufacturing.", "name": "Sam Pasupalak", "handle": "spisallyouneed", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1886850141065293824/XbWFJCXo_200x200.jpg", "likes": 15856, "rts": 2304, "replies": 793, "views": 4054470, "ts": 1792432716, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112239846702129152/vid/avc1/1280x720/tLYByn7SWDTLqqik.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112239846702129152/vid/avc1/3840x2160/QWb8Qsv5A_FWVppa.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112239846702129152/img/u4pwfHw4PjnRs2nc.jpg", "dur": 156}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null}, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Models & Labs", "score": 5.22, "thread": [], "tier": "worth"}]);